{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/628720-slashers-in-other-splats","id":628720,"title":"Slashers in other Splats.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-16T09:24:15-07:00","id":628720,"title":"Slashers in other Splats.","content":"How valid are slashers as villains in other splats?<br /> <br /> I dont think many kindred will approve of anyone but them terrorizing the mortals in their feeding ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T09:30:05-07:00","id":628742,"title":"","content":"Forget terrorising the mortals. A Slasher could easily be a danger to vampires. Imagine a Genius or a Harpy (see my sig) opposing a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T13:07:52-07:00","id":628979,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what Corvus Rex just said. Slashers are murder machines who will prey on any living thing around them, and who spiritually foul the area they're in through their depredations. A couple of sample storyhooks off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Vampires:<br /> * The city is in an uproar over a Slasher who has stylized itself as a &quot;vampire killer&quot; - the Damned need to find out who the leak is, be it a human psychopath or a rogue fledgling, and plug it.<br /> <br /> * A mortal important to one or more vampires has been threatened, attacked or killed by a slasher. This impudence cannot go unpunished.<br /> <br /> * A slasher is going after ghouls and even fledgling vampires, attempting to murder them and drink their blood because of a delusional belief that this will give it superpowers and/or immortality.<br /> <br /> <br /> Werewolves:<br /> * Werewolves become aware of a slasher's presence in their territory when spirits of pain, fear, murder, death and bloodshed begin multiplying out of control.A Hunt must be called to stem this flow of corruption.<br /> <br /> * A choice territory becomes the site of a battlefield between a werewolf pack and slashers, either a Brute or Mask or a feral clan of Freaks and/or Mutants. The werewolves could be defending themselves, or invaders, or even just neighbors who never noticed each other until now.<br /> <br /> * A Locus of particularly dark nature has come into being in the private den of a slasher. Do the werewolves try to take the locus for themselves, tap it in secret, or snuff it out as &quot;not worth the cost&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> Mages:<br /> * Mages become aware of a slasher's presence and identity when Death magics bring them into contact with a growing number of ghosts killed by a slasher.<br /> <br /> * Mages attempt to research the possible magical origins of a Scourge Undertaking slasher, such as a Mask or a Legend. What can possibly go wrong?<br /> <br /> * Mages become aware of a Hallow, a sarira, or other magically important spot or location that is guarded by a Scourge Slasher.<br /> <br /> <br /> Changelings:<br /> * Pressure comes down on the Autumn Court when it appears one of their members has gotten so caught up in its fear-mongering that they have taken to murdering humans. The true culprit, unbeknownst to the changelings, is a Slasher who has picked up on the Autumn Court-spread legends and has made them key to its motif. Can the changelings find the truth before the Avenger manages to meld with the weavings of Fate and become a full-fledged Legend?<br /> <br /> <br /> Prometheans:<br /> * The throng encounters a promethean created by a mortal demiurge - a slasher, who becomes even more obsessed with making more &quot;children&quot; after meeting them.<br /> <br /> * A promethean discovers its attempts to create a child are being mimicked by a slasher that has seen its efforts at &quot;harvesting&quot; and &quot;preparing&quot; corpses.<br /> <br /> * A Cobalus promethean becomes a voyeuristic protector to a slasher, seeking to understand the true depths of human evil and depravity as represented by this monster.<br /> <br /> * A promethean or throng finds itself protecting humans from a slasher that gleefully turns its future victims against their would-be protector(s).<br /> <br /> * A promethean or throng contemplating murdering to produce progeny is given another look at themselves when they discover a slasher with similar motives.<br /> <br /> * A particularly depraved slasher's experiments with the corpses of his victims are producing pandorans.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters:<br /> * Sin-eaters realise a slasher is in the area when hordes of ex-victim ghosts come flocking to them. They have to stop the slasher or be driven mad.<br /> <br /> * A sin-eater's geist recognizes a slasher as responsible for its original death and demands revenge.<br /> <br /> * One or more sin-eaters died at a slasher's hands, either before or after the Bargain. It's payback time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mummies:<br /> * A mummy realises that a slasher has infiltrated their cult - or that one of their cultists has turned into a slasher.<br /> <br /> * A nomadic mummy's cult awakens its master for protection when their travels bring them through the territory of one or more feral slashers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Demons:<br /> * A demon makes a Soul Pact for the life of a slasher - do they continue with the murderous original's ways, or do they try and cling to sanity at the cost of eroding their precious Cover?<br /> <br /> * Someone a demon cares about becomes victimised by a slasher.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone:<br /> * A slasher with a penchant for prolonged torture has taken you as a captive. Escape or fight your way free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T03:10:13-07:00","id":645203,"title":"","content":"I had as an idea that didn't come to fruition in a mage game that there was a left handed cabal that experimented on human psychopaths and through mind and life warped people into slashers and released them on the populace in order to wrack up a a high death and sense of fear and dread In the city. <br /> <br /> The point was to use the spirits this attracted to call forth a demon of great power from the depths and have him enter the world where the cabal wanted with the intention of chaining him. <br /> <br /> My game kind of petered out but that was the back story that I had intended for the players to discover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","name":"Slimjimjohnson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T17:31:58-07:00","id":647446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/628720-slashers-in-other-splats#post628720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How valid are slashers as villains in other splats?</div> </div> </div> </div>Answer: Very. A slasher has one trick, but he's good at it. It's being very good at making other people dead and getting away with it (with the exception of Avengers-Working the Room is kind of a crappy talent).<br /> <br /> Anyone a serial killer might decide needs to die is at risk when a slasher comes a-calling. That includes those touched by supernature. Even indirectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T22:05:48-07:00","id":658925,"title":"","content":"My ST loves using slashers, the problem is everyone but him prefers to play Mage over Vampire and Hunter. In Mage we tend to curbstomp even Masks. If we can't one shot them we capture them and drop them somewhere they can't bother us. So far its been deserted islands, pocket dimensions, The Shadow, another mage's house, or our Vampire character's city. We tend to throw stuff at our other characters in both games. Its become a running gag where we throw slashers and cursed weapons into the city our Vamps run and they in turn destroy the Princes haven. (I think his havens been destroyed 10 times now.) Our Vampires struggle with Masks heavily though and we are all Elders/Primogens/Prince. When we do go to fight things only two of us can fight the Masks and it tends to be me and a primogen that owns a flamethrower. His way of fighting is lighting everything on fire and running away screaming. Mine is to fight mono e mono with Sword cane, Celerity, Vigor, and my Ordo ability that makes me not Roshrek from fire and take low damage from fire. So yeah, generally ends with us taking Agg and the Slasher running off to chop up the Princes car or blow up his house, again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T12:57:09-07:00","id":659745,"title":"","content":"RAW, you CANNOT oneshot a mask. Unless you drop them in a volcano, or some other extremely hostile environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:01:47-07:00","id":659844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/628720-slashers-in-other-splats?p=647446#post647446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Answer: Very. A slasher has one trick, but he's good at it. It's being very good at making other people dead and getting away with it (with the exception of Avengers-Working the Room is kind of a crappy talent).<br /> <br /> Anyone a serial killer might decide needs to die is at risk when a slasher comes a-calling. That includes those touched by supernature. Even indirectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've reworked Avengers to give a +3 dice bonus on anyone they actively plan on killing with either firearms, chemicals, or explosives. -3 on a target of which doesn't fit their method of operation.<br /> <br /> note that collateral damage doesn't bump off the + 3 bonus. Getting to kill a single vampire justifies rigging the entire store to blow up and killing any people within or beside it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T16:31:16-07:00","id":660041,"title":"","content":"The one shot thing was meant to be in general, I know masks can't be. That's our mages answer for everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T02:22:15-07:00","id":665474,"title":"","content":"That said, one thing a Storyteller has to accept by running Slasher vs. Supernatural is that, if it comes down to a fight, Supernaturals have a lot of ways of making things <b>dead</b>. Especially those who've been beefed up by 2e.<br /> <br /> My advice is to embrace this going in. Don't get too attached to your Slasher, and don't be surprised if your vampires or werewolves decide that they want to rip your Leatherface or Michael Myers or Freddy apart once they corner him. It's called Catharsis, and will probably be more popular with your players than just dues ex machinaing him/her out of there. They'll remember the story much more fondly, and even if they do talk happily about how they ripped the Slasher apart, they'll also be more willing to fondly recall how you frightened them with him. As opposed to mocking you for running a lowbrow Slasher Movie expy and how they all hated it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T03:19:54-07:00","id":665500,"title":"","content":"Well, slashers have a tendency to come back as revenants, so killing them just gives the ST the right to upgrade then and then send the after you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}